{
  "quizzes": [
    {
      "question_text": "Solve for f. $$ \\\\[1em] 4 + \\frac{1}{3}f = 6 + f \\\\[1em] f=$$",
      "question_type": "Fill in the blank",
      "question_number": "1_1",
      "tag": "Gr8_100_E2",
      "correct_answers": [
        "-3"
      ],
      "solution": [
        [
          "1/4",
          "Multiply every term by $$3$$ to eliminate the fractions. $$\\\\[0.5em]$$ $$3(4) + 3 \\times \\frac{1}{3}f = 3(6) + 3f$$"
        ],
        [
          "2/4",
          "Simplify each term: $$\\\\[0.5em]$$ $$12 + f = 18 + 3f$$"
        ],
        [
          "3/4",
          "Move all terms with $$f$$ to one side and constants to the other side. $$\\\\[0.5em]$$ $$f - 3f = 18 - 12$$ $$\\\\[0.5em]$$ $$-2f = 6$$"
        ],
        [
          "4/4",
          "Divide both sides by $$-2$$: $$\\\\[0.5em]$$ $$f = 6 \\div -2$$ $$\\\\[0.5em]$$ $$f = -3$$"
        ]
      ],
      "solution_image_tag": [],
      "skill": "solve-linear-equations-with-variables-on-both-sides-fractions"
    },
